+## Stage-53 applicability correction (2026-10-20)
+
+The procedure and native-17 identity below remain historical. Do not apply its
+1:100 / 1.5 Ω CT arithmetic to stage 53. The inspected stage-53 board
+`worktrees/runs-native21/s53/c53int/section.kicad_pcb` has SHA-256
+`82af7bd93e62d1f2e6c7c2c2b971a4830bf6e09078bae3f269d8bead9a31fd27`:
+T1 Value/MPN are CST3015-200ED (1:200), and R39 is RC1206FR-073RL (3 Ω).
+The footprint description and provisional STEP filename still mention -100ED;
+those metadata are not the electrical part identity.
+
+Coilcraft CST3015 document 1608-1, revised 2025-09-08, lists 5.94 Ω maximum
+secondary DCR, 12.8 mH nominal secondary inductance (±25%) and 1276 V·µs for
+-200ED. Its 87 A listing describes the specified 40°C temperature-rise test,
+not an absolute saturation-current boundary. For the stage-53 CT, use the
+estimated induced secondary voltage `I/200 × (3 + 5.94) Ω` and integrate the
+entire actual shot. At 37 A, ideal 50 V linear ramps consume approximately
+61.2 / 153.0 / 611.9 V·µs for 100 / 250 / 1000 µH; each 10 µs at constant
+37 A adds approximately 16.54 V·µs. Half of 1276 is 638 V·µs, but that is a
+comparison with the historical half-rating convention, not a newly approved
+pulse limit or permission to reuse the native-17 fixture on stage 53.
+
+The rough RL reset estimate `12.8 mH / 8.94 Ω = 1.43 ms` uses nominal L
+and maximum DCR; it is not a worst-case reset-time bound. Re-establish reset
+with the assembled secondary, including capacitor/clamp dynamics and initial
+flux, rather than carrying forward a fixed 10 ms wait. Preserve the original
+native-13 model and native-17 calculation below when reproducing their results.
+A stage-53 test needs its own fixture mapping, model, pulse budget and evidence.
+
+Source: https://www.coilcraft.com/getmedia/df31d5fe-b3af-4586-82a7-7b773ac9f838/cst3015.pdf
 
